-- title:
--   Infinite Relaxed Energy Outside The Closure Domain
-- statement:
--   This theorem identifies the relaxed energy away from the domain of a closed operator.
--
--   Let $X$ be a real normed space, let $H$ be a complete real Hilbert space, and let $T:X\dashrightarrow H$ be closable. If $x\in X$ does not belong to the domain of the closure $\overline T$, then the sequential relaxation of the pre-energy generated by $T$ is infinite:
--
--   $$
--    x\notin\operatorname{dom}(\overline T)
--   \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
--   \operatorname{sequentialRelaxation}_{T}(x)=\top.
--   $$
--
--   The value $\top$ is the top element of `ENNReal`, namely $+\infty$. The declaration is `sequentialRelaxation_ofLinearPMap_of_notMem`; it makes no assertion about points inside the closure domain.
-- source:
--   Lean source: https://github.com/human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean/blob/408915f/formalization/FunctionalInequalities/Energy/Relaxation/LinearPMap.lean#L337-L355 (repository human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean, commit 408915f, module `FunctionalInequalities.Energy.Relaxation.LinearPMap`, declaration `FunctionalInequalities.Energy.PreEnergy.sequentialRelaxation_ofLinearPMap_of_notMem`; the repository is private at upload time).

